      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are correct. The problem is occurring during PR_Swap to sink after receiving Source_Cap. pd_is_vbus_present() returns 0 between DFP:Request and UFP:Accept and this is what\u0027s causing the state machine to enter the SNK_DISCONNECTED state and generating the Hard Reset when Accept is finally received.\n\nSink:UFP\t[3]PR_Swap\nSource:DFP\t[3]GoodCRC\nSource:DFP\t[4]Accept\nSink:UFP\t[4]GoodCRC\nSource:DFP\t[5]PS_RDY\nSink:UFP\t[5]GoodCRC\nSource:UFP\t[0]PS_RDY\nSource:DFP\t[0]GoodCRC\nSource:UFP\t[1]Source_Cap\nSink:DFP\t[1]GoodCRC\nSink:DFP\t[0]Request\nSource:UFP\t[0]GoodCRC\nSource:UFP\t[2]Accept\nSink:DFP\t[2]GoodCRC\nHard Reset\n\nI tracked the problem to bd9995x_select_input_port(). When writing to the VIN_CTRL_SET register, pd_is_vbus_present() return 0 for ~16mS even though VBUS is present.",
